.TH LOGLENS 1 "October 2026" "v1.0.0" "LogLens AI Manual"
.SH NAME
loglens \- autonomous, OS-aware Linux sysadmin and security copilot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B loglens
[\fI"task or error description"\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B LogLens AI
is an environment-aware terminal copilot and multimodal log auditor. It captures real-time host telemetry (distribution, kernel, package managers, and architecture) to synthesize non-interactive bash remediations, executing them on-demand via human-in-the-loop safeguards.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B Interactive REPL (No arguments)
Running \fBloglens\fR without arguments initializes an interactive terminal shell that persists across queries.
.TP
.B Single-Shot Execution (With query)
Running \fBloglens "command"\fR processes the request immediately, prompts for confirmation, and returns to the host shell.
.SH SPECIAL COMMANDS (REPL)
.TP
.B clear
Clears the terminal screen and redraws the telemetry dashboard.
.TP
.B help
Displays quick syntax references and command tips.
.TP
.B exit\fR, \fBquit
Terminates the interactive session.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/os-release
Queried to resolve host distribution identity.
.SH AUTHOR
Saad Shaikh (LogLens AI Project)
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report bugs and open issues at the project repository.
